      "source": "memory",
      "snippet": "[The SQL standard](https://www.iso.org/standard/63556.html) defines two basic instructions describing this mechanism: `SAVEPOINT` and extension to the `ROLLBACK` statement – `ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT`: ```undefined <savepoint statement> ::= SAVEPOINT <savepoint specifier> <savepoint specifier> ::= <savepoint name> <rollback statement> ::= ROLLBACK [ WORK ] [ AND [ NO ] CHAIN ] [ <savepoint clause> ]<savepoint clause> ::= TO SAVEPOINT <savepoint specifier> ``` Copy It also defines `RELEASE SAVEPOINT` that allows erasing information about an \"active\" savepoint: ```undefined <release savepoint statement> ::= RELEASE SAVEPOINT <savepoint specifier> ``` Copy PostgreSQL supp",
